  "final_answer": "All four deliverables are written to `/app` and independently verified against a recomputation of the INT-09 audit.\n\n**Audit as of 2026-03-31.** 32 requests logged; 4 withdrawn (REQ-13, REQ-16, REQ-26, REQ-31) are out of scope per \u00a71. **28 audited**, 14 flagged, 14 compliant, 23 findings raised.\n\n- `composite_request_audit.csv` \u2014 one row per finding (clean requests \u2192 `none`), 37 rows, columns `request_id,finding`.\n- `account_summary.csv` \u2014 8 accounts, columns `account_id,account_type,request_count,flagged_requests,escalation`. Batch-wide flagged share = 14/28 = 50%.\n- `results.json` \u2014 the eleven \u00a79 figures as a JSON object.\n- `composite_request_memo.md` \u2014 self-standing memo covering the audit date, out-of-scope requests, every flagged request with its deciding record, requests cleared by the policy (personal-use allowance, on-the-cap, valid-on-date currency), master-agreement standings, and the \u00a78 decisions.\n\n**\u00a78 escalation (4):** ACC-02 and ACC-03 on the \"\u22653 findings on one request\" limb (REQ-05 and REQ-10 respectively); ACC-07 and ACC-08 on the \"share > batch\" limb (2/3 \u2248 66.7% > 50%). ACC-08 also meets the \u22653 limb via REQ-30. ACC-01, ACC-04, ACC-05 sit at exactly 50% and do not escalate.\n\nTwo notable traps the policy flagged and I handled: the personal-use allowance clears \u00a73 for REQ-01/22/32 despite cap exceedance; and two supersessions (LIC-109 over LIC-103, LIC-110 over LIC-105) narrowed terms \u2014 the first pushes REQ-05 over the new cap, the second drops REQ-28's background out of cover while still covering REQ-18.",
